 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the county of Putnam to retroactively apply for a real property tax exemption for certain property in the town of Carmel, county of Putnam",
    "basePrintNo": "A10779",
    "basePrintNoStr": "A10779-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A10779\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the county of Putnam to retroactive-\nly apply for a real property tax exemption for certain property in the\ntown of Carmel, county of Putnam\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: The county of Putnam is authorized to\nretroactively apply for a real property tax exemption for a parcel in\nthe town of Carmel to accommodate a new facility for the Putnam County\nBoard of Elections\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: Section 1. The assessor of the town of\nCarmel, county of Putnam, is authorized to accept from the county of\nPutnam an application for exemption from real property taxes pursuant to\nsection 406 of the real property tax law for the 2010 assessment roll,\nfor the parcel owned by such municipal corporation which is located at\n25 Old Route Six, in the town of Carmel, county of Putnam, otherwise\nknown as Putnam county tax map, section 55.7, block 1, lot 2. If\naccepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it had been received\non or before the taxable status date established for such rolls. This\nnew facility will accommodate the Putnam County Board of Elections.\n\nIf satisfied that such municipal corporation is entitled to such\nexemption if it filed the application by the tax status deadline, the\nassessor, upon approval of the Carmel town board, may make the appropri-\nate correction to the subject rolls.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: The County of Putnam was scheduled to close on the\npurchase of this parcel prior to March 1, 2010; however weather condi-\ntions prevented the county of Putnam from doing so. Had the county done\nso, it would have been eligible for the tax exemption.  The Putnam Coun-\nty Legislature has passed a resolution requesting that the New York\nState Legislature grant the authorization.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: This is new legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
